      },
      "title": "Meet Hono",
      "description": "**New idea — Hono:** a small web framework for building APIs. You create an `app`, add *middleware* that runs on every request, and attach *routes* that answer specific addresses.\n\n**How it works:** this file imports one route file per feature (chat, providers, billing, …) and creates the main `app`. Each route file is its own small Hono app, mounted later in this file.\n\n**Why it matters:** this is the whole server side of the Next.js app, except the agent. Every `/api/...` call from the browser ends up here.\n\n**Watch out:** this same file can also run on its own with Bun (the last step of this file shows how). That's how it ran before Feb 9."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/server/index.ts",
      "line": 40,
      "selection": {
