          "line": 40,
          "character": 4
        }
      },
      "title": "Middleware, and why this runs lazily",
      "description": "**New idea — middleware:** `app.use(\"*\", fn)` runs `fn` for every request. Calling `await next()` passes the request on to the next middleware or the route.\n\n**How it works:** on the very first request, this starts Sentry (error tracking) and analytics, then never again.\n\n**Why it matters:** Next.js prerenders pages at build time and loads this module while doing it. Starting Sentry at load time caused crypto errors during prerendering, so it waits for a real request.\n\n**Watch out:** the flag is a plain variable. On Vercel, each new server instance starts with it reset, which is fine because each instance should initialise once."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/server/index.ts",
      "line": 53,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 46,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 53,
          "character": 31
        }
      },
      "title": "Timing, logging and security headers",
      "description": "**How it works:** three ready-made middlewares from Hono:\n- `timing()` adds a `Server-Timing` header showing how long the request took.\n- `logger()` prints each request and its status to the server log.\n- `secureHeaders()` adds standard browser security headers (for example, against clickjacking).\n\n**Why it matters:** cheap, standard protection and visibility for every endpoint.\n\n**Watch out:** order matters. These run before the routes, so even failed requests get logged."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/server/index.ts",
      "line": 100,
