          "character": 3
        }
      },
      "title": "CORS",
      "description": "**New idea — CORS:** browsers block a page from calling an API on a *different* address unless the API says that address is allowed. This block is that permission list.\n\n**How it works:** allowed: your production domain, localhost, and Vercel preview URLs that contain the project name or `sumanth-prasads-projects`. It also allows the `Authorization`, `x-stack-access-token` and `x-organization-id` headers.\n\n**Why it matters:** since Feb 9, pages and API share one address, so normal page calls don't need CORS at all. It still matters for preview deployments and other callers.\n\n**Watch out:** for an unknown origin, the code returns the *first* allowed origin instead of the caller's. That doesn't match, so the browser blocks the call. It works, but it's an unusual way to say no."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/server/index.ts",
      "line": 112,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 102,
          "character": 1
        },
