          "line": 112,
          "character": 4
        }
      },
      "title": "Error handler and an unreachable route",
      "description": "**How it works:** `errorHandler` catches anything thrown in a route and turns it into a clean JSON error. The `app.get(\"/\")` route answers a health check at the root.\n\n**Why it matters:** routes can just `throw` (like `HTTPException(401)` in the auth check) and the user still gets a tidy response.\n\n**Watch out:** inside Next.js, only `/api/...` reaches Hono, so this root `/` route can never be hit. It's left over from when this ran as its own server on Render."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/server/index.ts",
      "line": 152,
      "selection": {
