          "line": 152,
          "character": 24
        }
      },
      "title": "Mounting every route under /api",
      "description": "**New idea — sub-apps:** `api.route(\"/chat\", chatRoutes)` attaches a whole route file under a prefix. A route written as `/session` in `chat.ts` becomes `/api/chat/session`.\n\n**How it works:** all features are mounted on `api`, and `api` is mounted on `app` at `/api`. So `providers.ts` answers `/api/providers/...`, `internal.ts` answers `/api/internal/...`, and so on.\n\n**Why it matters:** this list is the table of contents of your API. Each line is one file in `routes/`.\n\n**Watch out:** `/api/test-auth` is mounted in every environment. The comment says it's only *enabled* in CI or test environments, so the check must live inside that route file."
    },
