        }
      },
      "title": "Connecting to the database",
      "description": "**New idea — ORM:** Drizzle lets you write database queries in TypeScript (`db.insert(chatSessions)...`) instead of SQL strings, with types checked for you.\n\n**How it works:** `neon(...)` uses Neon's serverless driver, which sends queries over HTTP. That suits Vercel, where servers start and stop all the time. The `Proxy` creates the connection only on first use.\n\n**Why it matters:** during `next build`, `DATABASE_URL` may not exist. Connecting lazily stops the build from crashing.\n\n**Watch out:** a `Proxy` is unusual. Every `db.something` access goes through the `get` trap, which binds functions to the real database object."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/server/db/schema.ts",
      "line": 203,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 191,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 203,
          "character": 4
        }
      },
      "title": "A table, written in code",
      "description": "**How it works:** `pgTable(\"chat_sessions\", {...})` describes a Postgres table: each column with its type and rules (`notNull`, `default`). The second part adds indexes to make lookups by user, organisation and date fast.\n\n**Why it matters:** the same definition gives you the table, the TypeScript types, and the query builder. `bun run db:push` applies it to the database.\n\n**Watch out:** `userId` points at Neon Auth's users, but there's no foreign key (the comment says so). The database won't stop a chat from pointing at a deleted user."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/server/db/schema.ts",
      "line": 173,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 147,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 173,
          "character": 4
        }
      },
      "title": "Where your Google tokens live",
      "description": "**What it is:** one row per connected AdMob or Ad Manager account.\n\n**How it works:** it stores the account's id (`publisherId` or `networkCode`) and the Google OAuth tokens. The tokens are **encrypted** (JWE) before saving, using the key in `TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_SECRET` (`lib/crypto.ts`).\n\n**Why it matters:** these tokens let the agent act on your ad account. Encrypting them means a leaked database dump isn't enough to use them.\n\n**Watch out:** the comment on this table still says `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET`, which is out of date. Also, this file still defines the old Better Auth tables (`users`, `sessions`, …) and CrewAI tables (`crew_agents`, `crew_tasks`) that the current code no longer uses for login or agents. The OAuth tour covers connecting accounts."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/server/routes/chat.ts",
      "line": 54,
